{"returncode":0,"stdout":"This start of a new chat is the continuity of the building of the TF RiskManager EA script that will run on the Meta Trader 5 (MT5) trading platform. The attached version (v14.32) of the EA script still has bugs to fix. The attached image shows the triggering of a Daily Loss Limit (DLL) alert due to a miscalculation of the DLL Buffer. This DLL Buffer is displayed on the GUI output panel under Risks. It calculation is wrong as evidenced by the actual daily gain for this day. Please review and fix the coding related to this DLL calculation issue.TF-RiskManager-v14.32.mq5✅ Fixed — DLL Buffer & Risk Critical Alerts
The bug was a copy-paste / logic error in the buffer calculation:

Buffer_DLL (and the 80% warning logic that uses it) was incorrectly using HighWaterMark (TLL-style trailing peak) instead of PriorDayClose (the true daily reset point).
When price pulled back from an intra-day high, HighWaterMark stayed elevated → Buffer_DLL collapsed to a tiny value (e.g. $119.80) even though you had + $465 daily gain.
This triggered false “RISK CRITICAL [DLL]: >80% consumed” alerts and showed the wrong “DLL Buffer” / “Eff Risk Buf [DLL]” in the panel.

